  "id": "COMPOUND:35932 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "(+)-Caryolan-1-ol is implicated in the interaction with Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a series of molecular targets that share a common pathway. The evidence suggests that (+)-Caryolan-1-ol acts as a target for SNB-78 and 12-O-Deacetyl-12-Epi-19-Deoxy-22-Hydroxyscalarin, both of which are themselves targets of Hepatocyte and Cocosamide B, respectively. This implies a potential cascade of interactions where (+)-Caryolan-1-ol may influence the activity of these targets, which in turn affect Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The presence of multiple targets in this pathway suggests that the relationship between (+)-Caryolan-1-ol and Replicase polyprotein 1ab is likely mediated through a network of downstream effectors, possibly through enzyme inhibition or regulatory mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions, with the final link to Replicase polyprotein 1ab being supported by the cumulative evidence across the visible paths.",
